#17764
Grand Ballroom~
Dancing, laughter, lights, music, people, parties, drinks, food.  All the
things life should be, once...  Long ago.  But no more.  Not in this room or
any room in this old mansion.  Not since the soldiers came.  Not since the
murders of the family of Leah.  Once proud room, now nothing but a storage
house for murders.  Once a gay place, filled with dancing and music and
laughter, now filled with the haunting memories of screams as blades drank deep
and only a few survived.    
~
