#17767
Old bedroom~
This appears to be the master bedroom for a glorious old brass bed, now
tarnished, lies propped up against a vanity.  The bed itself is covered in
lovely red and white sheets.  The vanity is finely decorated with a scawling
design the carpenter must have made while making.  You move further in, taken
by what appears to be a room missed and passed over by the murder and chaos in
the rest of the upstairs.  But wait, the sheets, that isn't dye on them.  The
sheets are covered in blood.  Human blood for the bodies lie festering and
decaying under the blankets.  You look toward the vanity.  The designs are claw
marks you suddenly realize.  What could have done this?  The hair once more
begins to rise yet no sound can be heard, no motion sensed or felt.    
~
